    {
      "id": "tlrvto8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Maratha Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Shivaji Maharaj (1630–1680) was the founder and central figure of the Maratha Empire.",
        "The Maratha rise involved early conquests and significant military conflicts with the Mughal Empire.",
        "Shivaji established well-defined administrative, military, and revenue systems.",
        "The Maratha Empire saw major expansion after Shivaji's period before its eventual decline."
      ],
      "id": "xvqn6ia"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4m83zir",
      "content": "• The Marathas lived in the Deccan region of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6gh0dwv",
      "content": "• They were mainly farmers and warriors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "up4356u",
      "content": "• The weakening of the Deccan Sultanates and Mughal authority helped the rise of Maratha power."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g2r3hf4",
      "content": "• Shivaji organized the Marathas into a strong military and political force."
    },
    {
      "id": "l0a6j0e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Shivaji Maharaj (1630–1680)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6owhw2t",
      "content": "Shivaji was the founder of the Maratha Empire and one of the greatest rulers in Indian history."
    },
